<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Léon Humblot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1914">1914</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Léon Humblot was a French naturalist and adventurer who went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-comore">Grande Comore</a> in 1884 to collect plants. He backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-ali-bin-said-omar">Said Ali of Bambao</a> as sultan of the whole island, and in 1886 obtained both a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and a concession over much of the island's land. He served for years as French resident and ran large plantations of vanilla and other crops.</p></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Léon Joseph Henry Humblot was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a> on 3 June 1852. He worked as a gardener for the Muséum national d'histoire naturelle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, and in 1878 he set out on a research journey to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, where he laid out an experimental garden and collected orchids. In 1884 he went to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a> as part of a geographical survey organised by the museum.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p>On <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-comore">Grande Comore</a> he obtained a treaty with the sultan of Bambao that laid the ground for a French protectorate over the island, and within a short time the French held overall rule of Grande Comore, Anjouan, Mayotte and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moheli">Mohéli</a>. Humblot founded a colonial company on the island that ran several farms and plantations and factories processing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a> and perfumes. He held the title of Résident from 1889 to 1896, when the French government forced him to give it up on charges of corruption.</p><p>In 1885 a set of 66 photographs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a>, Nossi-Bé and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> was given by Alphonse Milne-Edwards; taken by Humblot, they include portraits of Said Ali, sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-comore">Grande Comore</a>, his ministers and brothers, princesses of the island, and Humblot himself as French resident.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Works and ideas</h2><p>Throughout his years in the Comoros Humblot collected botanical specimens and sent them to the naturalist Alfred Grandidier (1836-1921). The herbarium of the museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> received many items from him, among them 1,300 specimens of vascular plants, and he also collected birds and insects. The plant genera Humblotia, Humblotiella and Humblotiodendron are named after him, as are Humblot's heron, Humblot's flycatcher and Humblot's sunbird. He died on 20 March 1914.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Léon Humblot” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Said Ali of Bambao, backed by the French adventurer <b>Leon Humblot</b>, became paramount and in 1886 signed a French protectorate over the whole island.</blockquote><a href="/state/sultanate-of-bambao">Sultanate of Bambao</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Nancy, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in Mitsamiouli, in what is now <a href="/countries/comoros">the Comoros</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.69,6.18&amp;year=1892" aria-label="Nancy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the birthplace of Léon Humblot"><image href="/maps/globes/g000n60.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5348 5944h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5348 5944h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.69,6.18&amp;year=1892">What was here in 1892? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
